model {
  extend basalt.frameworkRelease {
    metadata {
      constraint "Every host build embeds all canonical and qualified production framework identities plus its checked producer before bundling. Only the trusted release records a candidate-bound producer qualification with exact runtime.json and framework.json hashes in the existing production deployment ledger before activation. Production rereads both files and verifies their identical runtime bytes, the exact producer, complete history and generated registry before recording. Failed or unknown activation never removes qualification; later hosts retain all earlier qualified identities. Both approved pre-enrollment releases are canonical qualifications with distinct release-log-bound reproducible-build source revisions and never claim a serving-byte match. Canonical build inputs remain separate from the generated runtime registry so Worker bundles embed history once. Compact generated storage decodes to the identical ordered publication tuples and hashes before admission. App builds cannot enroll identities, and runtime admission remains offline and exact."
    }
  }
}
